# Business Rules Catalog

## Purpose
Centralized repository of business rules that govern the product's behavior. Every rule here is the single source of truth — if a rule contradicts a user story or process map, this catalog takes precedence.

## Rule Categories

### 1. User & Access Rules

| Rule ID | Rule Statement | Category | Trigger | Exceptions | Source |
|---------|---------------|----------|---------|------------|--------|
| UAR-001 | ... | Access Control | ... | ... | ... |

Cover:
- Registration and account creation rules
- Authentication requirements (password policy, MFA, session timeout)
- Role-based access control rules
- Account suspension/deletion rules
- Invitation and referral rules

### 2. Data Validation Rules

| Rule ID | Rule Statement | Category | Input Data | Outcome | Exceptions |
|---------|---------------|----------|-----------|---------|------------|
| DVR-001 | ... | Input Validation | ... | ... | ... |

Cover:
- Required fields and formats
- Data type constraints
- Cross-field validation (e.g., end date must be after start date)
- Uniqueness constraints
- Data sanitization rules

### 3. Business Logic Rules

| Rule ID | Rule Statement | Category | Trigger | Input | Outcome | Exceptions |
|---------|---------------|----------|---------|-------|---------|------------|
| BLR-001 | ... | Core Logic | ... | ... | ... | ... |

Cover:
- Core domain logic (the rules that make this business unique)
- Calculation rules (pricing, scoring, ranking algorithms)
- State transition rules (what status changes are allowed and when)
- Threshold and limit rules
- Prioritization and sorting rules

### 4. Pricing & Billing Rules

| Rule ID | Rule Statement | Category | Trigger | Conditions | Outcome |
|---------|---------------|----------|---------|------------|---------|
| PBR-001 | ... | Pricing | ... | ... | ... |

Cover:
- Pricing tier rules (what determines which tier a user is on)
- Discount rules (conditions, limits, approval requirements)
- Trial period rules
- Upgrade/downgrade rules
- Billing cycle rules
- Payment failure handling (retry schedule, grace period, suspension)
- Refund rules
- Tax and currency rules

### 5. Notification & Communication Rules

| Rule ID | Rule Statement | Category | Trigger | Channel | Timing |
|---------|---------------|----------|---------|---------|--------|
| NCR-001 | ... | Notification | ... | ... | ... |

Cover:
- When to send notifications (triggers)
- Channel selection rules (email vs push vs in-app vs SMS)
- Frequency limits (no more than X notifications per day)
- Opt-out/preference rules
- Escalation rules
- Digest/batching rules

### 6. Content & Moderation Rules

| Rule ID | Rule Statement | Category | Trigger | Action | Audit |
|---------|---------------|----------|---------|--------|-------|
| CMR-001 | ... | Content | ... | ... | ... |

Cover (if applicable):
- Content creation and editing rules
- Moderation policies
- Spam/abuse detection rules
- Content visibility rules
- Intellectual property rules

### 7. Integration & External System Rules

| Rule ID | Rule Statement | Category | System | Behavior | Fallback |
|---------|---------------|----------|--------|----------|---------|
| IER-001 | ... | Integration | ... | ... | ... |

Cover:
- Data synchronization rules (which system is source of truth)
- Conflict resolution rules (what happens when systems disagree)
- Rate limiting and throttling rules
- Fallback behavior when external systems are unavailable
- Data mapping and transformation rules

### 8. Compliance & Audit Rules

| Rule ID | Rule Statement | Category | Regulation | Requirement | Audit Trail |
|---------|---------------|----------|-----------|-------------|-------------|
| CAR-001 | ... | Compliance | ... | ... | ... |

Cover:
